# C1 end: the Shatter. The last scene of Chapter 1.
# Kaelen and Elara come through onto the Ironhold side, see the city, look back
# at Oakhaven (Aldric first, then the village meeting), and turn toward Ironhold.
# Replaces play_post_shatter_dialogue() in scripts/chapter1/ch1_shatter_transition.gd.
# Entry node: start.
# Elara is always with Kaelen here (elara_meeting.dlg keeps her in every branch),
# so there is no solo branch. She uses his name.
# It's night: Tobb is asleep (fragment_one.dlg) and after_kill says "It's not morning".
#
# Scene events (the scene implements these):
#   do pan_ironhold   camera pans over the city; hide the dialogue box. NEW.
#   do look_back      Kaelen turns toward Oakhaven. Once per path, in the Aldric node.
#   do pause 2.0      built in.
#
# Flag order (reads flags only; sets none):
#   1. Aldric, router "aldric": ch1_root_purge, then ch1_knight_killed, then
#      ch1_knight_spared, else after_none.
#      Purge also sets ch1_knight_spared (aldric.dlg), so it is checked first.
#      A kill also reads ch1_aldric_kill_owned / _justified / _unsure.
#      A save with no Aldric flag (made before the rewrite) gets after_none.
#   2. Village meeting, router "village": ch1_oakhaven_warned_villagers, then
#      ch1_oakhaven_warned_leaders, then ch1_oakhaven_left_quietly, else
#      village_none. fragment_one.dlg sets exactly one, so the order only matters
#      for old or broken saves.

~ start
Kaelen (Internal): Everything's heavier. My boots, my arms, the sword. Like the ground just remembered I'm standing on it.
Kaelen: Okay. Either the world just came apart and put itself back together, or I hit my head harder than I—
Elara: You didn't hit your head. I'd have heard it.
Elara: First time I came this way, I lost an hour in a ditch being sick. You're doing better than I did.
Kaelen (Internal): The air tastes like soot and hot copper, and there's steam hissing somewhere close that never stops for breath.
do pan_ironhold
Kaelen: That's Ironhold, isn't it? What are we walking into?
Elara: Work, mostly. Forges, caravan yards, a bell for every shift. They'll want to know who you are at the gate.
Kaelen: Then I hope they're patient. I'm still working that out myself.
=> aldric

~ aldric
[if ch1_root_purge] => after_purge
[if ch1_knight_killed] => after_kill
[if ch1_knight_spared] => after_spare
=> after_none

~ after_kill
do look_back
Kaelen (Internal): Somewhere behind that smoke is the gate he died guarding. It already looks smaller than it should.
Elara: You're doing it again. Staring.
Kaelen: He said "good". Right before. I keep trying to work out what he meant by it.
Elara: He meant it. Aldric never said anything he didn't mean, not even to be kind.
[if ch1_aldric_kill_owned] Kaelen: You told me not to dress it up. I'm not going to start now.
[if ch1_aldric_kill_justified] Kaelen: He was a threat. That's true, and it isn't enough, is it?
[if ch1_aldric_kill_unsure] Kaelen: You said it'd still be there in the morning. It's not morning, and it's still there.
Elara: Then carry it. Just don't carry it alone.
=> village

~ after_spare
do look_back
Kaelen (Internal): He's back there in his own village, still arguing with an order nobody else can hear.
Elara: He'll come back or he won't. Standing here won't decide it.
Kaelen: I know. I just wanted to be the last one who looked.
Elara: Oakhaven's stubborn. It'll keep an eye on him whether he likes it or not.
Kaelen: Okay. If he's still in there, the directive slips eventually. If he isn't—
Elara: Don't finish that. Not out loud.
=> village

~ after_purge
do look_back
Kaelen (Internal): He knew her name. He knew she was lying. That's two things the purge didn't take, and I don't know what it did.
Elara: He remembered me. I keep waiting to find out what he didn't.
Kaelen: I'm sorry. I couldn't tell you what it would cost, and I did it anyway.
Elara: You told me you didn't know. Before you did it. That's the part I'll hold on to.
Kaelen: And the rest of it?
Elara: Ask me in a week. Ask him, if he's the one who answers.
=> village

~ after_none
do look_back
Kaelen (Internal): Oakhaven's behind the smoke now. Everything I did there already feels like it happened to someone else.
Elara: It didn't. It happened to you, and to us. Keep walking.
=> village

# The village meeting (fragment_one.dlg, C1-S11). Each branch is short on purpose.
~ village
do pause 2.0
[if ch1_oakhaven_warned_villagers] => village_warned
[if ch1_oakhaven_warned_leaders] => village_leaders
[if ch1_oakhaven_left_quietly] => village_quiet
=> village_none

~ village_warned
Kaelen: I told Mara I'd find out about the wells. I said give me a day.
Elara: She'll have the whole village boiling water until you come back and tell her to stop.
Kaelen: Then I'd better come back with an answer.
=> under

~ village_leaders
Kaelen: Bran and Mara know. Tobb too, once Bran's woken him and put it in writing for him.
Kaelen: Three people out of a whole village. Was that enough, do you think?
Elara: Ask me after the council's met. Bran will have written down who said what.
=> under

# Elara answers him sideways. She doesn't use his name here, and that's on purpose.
~ village_quiet
Kaelen: You think I should have told them.
Elara: Tull and Wenna will be arguing about the water again by morning. Nobody's told them it was never the sluice.
=> under

~ village_none
Kaelen (Internal): Nobody back there knows what's under their village. I'm not sure I do either.
=> under

# What Kaelen knows by the end of Chapter 1: the shrine words, and one memory of
# arguing for seven signatures (fragment_one.dlg). Nothing more. No Human Patch yet.
~ under
Kaelen: Down in the shrine, those words on the wall. I knew them before I read them.
Elara: I remember. You went white.
Kaelen: Someone made it so nothing down there changes without seven signatures. I remember arguing for it.
Kaelen: If some of what's under Oakhaven is mine, I need to know which parts before I touch anything else.
Elara: Mara's bread is still Mara's bread, whoever laid the stones under her oven.
Elara: And if you start feeling guilty about it, don't you dare go fixing my arm to make up for it.
=> onward

~ onward
Kaelen: I probably wasn't going to.
Elara: Come on, Kaelen. It's further than it looks, and I'd like walls round us by morning.
Kaelen: Okay. Walls first. Then the list of names.
=> END
